    "attributes": {
        "action": "Mandate guidance on prioritising search areas with water for missing children",
        "additional_details": "We believe the risk is too high to not do something about this. \r\n\r\nDrowning is the number one cause of injury-related death for autistic children in the US. We believe the risk is too high to not do something about this. \r\nWhy the Risk is so High\r\nDrawn to Water: Autistic children often find water soothing or fascinating, leading them to seek it out without realizing the danger.\r\nLack of Awareness: Many children lack the skills to recognize hazards, swim safely, or understand deep water.\r\nElopement Triggers: Sensory overload, anxiety, or curiosity can cause a child to bolt suddenly from safe areas.\r\n \r\nSome families have lost their children as the risk is so high around water. This needs to be recognised in guidance.",
        "background": "Mandate guidance on prioritising search areas with water for missing children. Water can pose a particular risk for autistic children. According to the National Autism Association, accidental drowning accounts for roughly 71% of all lethal wandering incidents among individuals with autism.",
